{
  "task": "isaac_crank_pendulum",
  "axis": "cross-simulator-conversion-usd-isaac",
  "simulator": "pychrono",
  "source": "CONVERSION shape, Isaac Sim / USD (declarative): the prompt embeds a compact hand-authored USDA stage in Isaac's exact idiom (UsdPhysics revolute joints with per-body localPos frames, MassAPI mass/COM/diagonalInertia, PhysX DriveAPI; Z-up, metersPerUnit 1; angular drive targets in the schema's DEGREE units). MATCHED TRIPLE: the physics, constants, and bands are identical to pyb_arm_motor, so score differences between the imperative PyBullet task and this declarative USD task isolate pure representation effects (the pre-registered C15 instrument). Bands anchored to the same RK4 oracle (three-way validated on the PyBullet side to 4 decimals); the USDA is usd-core linted; its Isaac Sim replay is PENDING (NVIDIA machine), stated in CONTRACT.md",
  "scoring": {
    "weights": {"L1": 0.30, "L2": 0.20, "L3": 0.50},
    "invariant_fail_cap": 40
  },
  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
